Week01 Reflection
"Software" is a group of digital instructions that tell a computer or device how to behave or what to do. 
"Engineering is the use of science, maths, and technology to design, build, and solve real-world problems. 
"Software Engineering" is the application of engineering practices to manage software.
Some software that is used daily that is generally regarded as very easy to use would be google and WhatsApp. 
An example of a poorer piece of software which users generally try to avoid would be Microsoft teams. 

I work as a manager at a leisure centre, and the software we use to run our tills is the worst piece of software I have ever come across. 
Daily there is a system crash, and we are constantly having to apologize to customers for the delay of service.
something that the developers could have done differently to better improve the software is to optimize the local data syncing and background hardware integrations. 
This would be so that the software handles peak-hour gym traffic without freezing. 
They also could implement a stronger API rate-limiting and automated regressions testing. 
This would be to catch bugs before the system updates are rolled out.
